      "side": 1,
      "message": "I didn\u0027t really have a plan for supporting other sub-commands, but I had hoped to avoid forcing the tester to deal with `ec_params_typec_control` containing a union. This change gets rid of type-checking and forces the caller to know what size things are. Ways that might be a bit more high-level:\n* The remaining union members become function params. That\u0027s a bit verbose and forces the caller to specify placeholder values for multiple parameters. They also have to understand which params are used for which sub-command, but they\u0027d have to do that with other approaches as well.\n* Have the caller directly specify the `ec_params_typec_control`. This would break the pattern in this file, and I was trying to avoid it, but it would be essentially foolproof.\n* Give the union inside `ec_params_typec_control` a name and have a parameter of that type here. This would keep the function calls terse and high-level. The main downside would be giving a name to something we don\u0027t want people to use in most contexts.",
      "revId": "82859bdf2cb2f22552e1ca7c5f54b1e4b1df697e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
